Azure management and monitoring provide visibility into resource health, performance, configuration, and operational events. These capabilities allow administrators to detect problems and respond before they significantly affect users.

A management foundation can include:

* Azure Monitor
* Log Analytics
* Activity logs
* Alerts
* Resource health
* Application monitoring
* Operational dashboards

For example, an alert can notify an operations team when a production virtual machine experiences sustained high CPU utilization.

A real-life use case is an enterprise operations team monitoring thousands of Azure resources and receiving alerts when workloads deviate from expected behavior.

Centralized monitoring improves troubleshooting, reliability, and operational awareness.
